---
import { SitePage } from '@boombapbot/editor';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Stay Stoked, Stay Woke · boombapbot"
  description="A footnote to a drum machine app made by a white guy in tech, about whose music made these machines matter."
>
  <SitePage client:load baseUrl={base} current="manifesto" layout="note">
    <h1>Stay Stoked, Stay Woke</h1>
    <p>
      I want to add a little footnote to this drum machine app made by a white guy in tech (me) that offers a small
      paid tier. A lot of the reason anyone still cares about these machines is what Black musicians figured out how
      to do with them. You can hear house and techno all weekend without hearing much about the Black artists who
      built those scenes. And in hip-hop and dance music, white artists like the Beastie Boys and Diplo built hugely
      successful careers drawing on sounds that Black artists developed.
    </p>
    <p>
      There’s something familiar about how easily Black music, slang, and dances travel while Black kids get pushed
      into the school-to-prison pipeline and Black patients struggle to be heard in the health care system. I think
      about that when I put a price on an app built around sounds I love.
    </p>
  </SitePage>
</Base>
